proposed": "not run", "marker": "NOT_ADMISSIBLE", "harvest": "NEEDS_JUDGE", "reason": "pending slow clock", "provisional": true}, "topic_node": {"outcome": "ABSTAIN_LOW_CONFIDENCE", "answer_or_proposed": "medtop:08000000", "marker": "BELOW_BAR", "harvest": "LABEL_QUEUE"}}, "total_ms": 435.14, "over_budget": false, "seq": 24, "read_at": 1795289836.6545682, "lag_s": 80875.19, "gaps": ["WINDOW_CUT", "TOPIC_DISAGREE", "RERANK_DISAGREE", "LANDING_WEAK", "UNPLACED_HIGH", "DECIDER_ABSTAIN", "NOT_ATTACHED"]}, "text": "Exam shows that hat Fiona the hippo ate was deep into her small intestine. Following the death of Fiona the hippo, countless tributes have poured in for the beloved Cincinnati Zoo resident. Zoo officials shared an update on how those closest to her — her mother and brother — are doing. On Nov. 19, Fiona died at age 9 days after she swallowed a hat that accidentally landed in her enclosure. The normal lifespan of a hippo is 35 years, per the Cincinnati Zoo. Fiona is survived by her mother, Bibi, younger half-brother Fritz, who was born in 2022, and Tucker, Bibi’s mate. In an official statement released Nov. 20, the zoo’s Director of Animal Care Christina Gorsuch said Bibi, Fritz and Tucker are currently eating and behaving normally following the loss of Fiona. “It’s difficult to know how they’re feeling, but they appear to be their normal selves,” she said. Cincinnati Zoo’s Director of Animal Health Dr. Mike Wenninger also offered insight into the health struggles Fiona faced in her final days after accidentally ingesting a hat. A necropsy revealed that the hat was located in the middle of Fiona’s small intestine. “Upper and lower GI endoscopy were unable to reach the object,” he said. “The location and anatomy made laparoscopic removal impossible. No treatment aside from supportive care had any chance for success, and the necropsy confirmed that no amount of supportive care would have worked.” Fiona was born six weeks early in 2017, and she quickly became a viral hit after surviving the premature birth. As a newborn, Fiona weighed only 29 pounds, couldn’t stand on her own and required 24/7 care from the zoo. In recent years, the zoo has continued to share regular updates on her progress. The zoo remains open after her death, but the area directly around Hippo Cove will be closed through this weekend to give the animal care team “the space they need.” The zoo has experienced an outpouring of love from Fiona’s many fans. “We have received so much love from our community and beyond,” Zoo Director Dave Jenike said. “We were touched when we saw stadiums, bridges, and buildings lit in purple last night. The support that we’re feeling from all over the world reminds me of the time when everyone pulled together to root for her to survive. She did, and she gave us almost a decade of smiles.” The zoo also shared a message to Fiona’s most dedicated fans looking to honor the hippo who served as a symbol of resilience and hope. “In lieu of flowers, food, and material gifts, the Zoo is asking that people honor Fiona by spreading love and cheer to those around you,” the zoo said in a statement. **This story first appeared on TODAY.com. More from TODAY:**", "stages_full": {"windows": {"windows": 12, "cap": 12, "pct_body_read": 91, "offsets_text": [[75, 293], [293, 493], [494, 664], [664, 852], [852, 1052], [1052, 1229], [1230, 1455], [1455, 1651], [1651, 1870], [1871, 2050], [2051, 2269], [2269, 2452]]}, "scan_dates": {"spots": {"attribution": 5, "date": 2, "entity": 30, "event": 3, "modal": 1, "money": 1, "negation": 1, "quantity": 2, "quote": 7}, "dates": [["Nov. 19", "2026-11-19"], ["Nov. 20", "2026-11-20"]], "dates_resolved": 2, "anchor": "2026-11-20", "time_proxy": {"label": "time_proxy", "marker": "PROVISIONAL", "offset_days": [-1, 0], "n": 2, "of": "resolved date minus published date, in days"}}, "facts": {"kinds": {"amount": 6, "date": 2, "name": 30, "triple": 52}, "stated": 51, "unbound": 39, "invalid": 0, "stated_amount": 6, "